</div></div><p id=3D"92e9" class=3D"pw-post-body-paragraph oi oj jf ok b ol=
 om on oo op oq or os ot ou ov ow ox oy oz pa pb pc pd pe pf iz cv" data-se=
lectable-paragraph=3D"">APIs are fundamental to modern software, enabling s=
eamless communication across systems through defined protocols and architec=
tural styles like REST, SOAP, GraphQL, and gRPC. Their widespread use, howe=
ver, also creates a broad attack surface, making them susceptible to seriou=
s security issues such as data exposure, broken authentication, authorizati=
on flaws, injection attacks, and misconfigurations. To address these risks,=
 OWASP provides the API Security Top 10, highlighting critical vulnerabilit=
ies including Broken Object Level Authorization, Unrestricted Resource Cons=
umption, Server-Side Request Forgery, Improper Inventory Management, and Un=
safe Consumption of APIs. This module focuses on understanding and exploiti=
ng these weaknesses in RESTful APIs while emphasizing best practices to pre=
vent them in real-world environments.</p><blockquote class=3D"pg ph pi"><p =
id=3D"ec52" class=3D"oi oj pj ok b ol om on oo op oq or os ot ou ov ow ox o=
y oz pa pb pc pd pe pf iz cv" data-selectable-paragraph=3D"">For every exer=
cise, the first steps are to authenticate using the provided credentials, u=
se the JWT to authorize your session, and verify your assigned roles in the=
 Roles collection.</p></blockquote><h3 id=3D"5482" class=3D"pk pl jf z pm p=
n po ao pp pq pr aq ps ot pt pu pv ox pw px py pb pz qa qb qc cv" data-sele=
ctable-paragraph=3D"">Broken Object Level Authorization</h3><p id=3D"12cb" =
class=3D"pw-post-body-paragraph oi oj jf ok b ol qd on oo op qe or os ot qf=
 ov ow ox qg oz pa pb qh pd pe pf iz cv" data-selectable-paragraph=3D"">Web=
 APIs often rely on user-supplied identifiers like UUIDs or integers to fet=
ch resources, but if the backend fails to properly enforce object-level aut=
horisation, it leads to Broken Object Level Authorisation (BOLA/IDOR). In t=
his scenario, a Supplier user logs into the Inlanefreight Marketplace API a=
nd retrieves their JWT, company ID, and assigned roles. One role =E2=80=94 =
=E2=80=9CSupplierCompanies_GetYearlyReportByID=E2=80=9D allows access to a =
yearly-report endpoint that incorrectly takes an integer ID without verifyi=
ng that the requested report belongs to the authenticated user=E2=80=99s co=
mpany. As a result, the user can access other companies=E2=80=99 confidenti=
al yearly reports simply by changing the ID value.</p><p id=3D"f3e1" class=
=3D"pw-post-body-paragraph oi oj jf ok b ol om on oo op oq or os ot ou ov o=
w ox oy oz pa pb pc pd pe pf iz cv" data-selectable-paragraph=3D"">This vul=
nerability allows not only unauthorised access to individual reports but al=
so mass exploitation by automating ID enumeration through scripting. The co=
re issue is missing server-side authorisation checks that should compare th=
e report=E2=80=99s companyID with the supplier=E2=80=99s authenticated comp=
anyID. To prevent BOLA, the API must enforce strict object-level permission=
 checks to ensure users can access only the data belonging to their own org=
anisation.</p><pre class=3D"qi qj qk ql qm qn qo qp ie qq cn cv"><span id=
=3D"9bae" class=3D"qr pl jf qo b cr qs qt e qu qv" data-selectable-paragrap=
